Well, it's cheating and you're more likely to learn from a bad mistake
(falling carrying a 'trice corpse or whatever) when it really has game-
ending impact.  If all you care about is getting better at the real
thing, I'd suggest:

1. Play on NAO so that others can kibbitz and you can ask for help in
IRC
2. Play the whole game through once in explore mode so you know the
basic outline and what's required
3. Spoil yourself silly

But I'd recommend just playing the game (no explore, only what
spoilers you find yourself aching for) for quite a while first;
discovering bits and pieces on your own is quite fun, IMO!


